          "filename": "Chile-02624 - Fish Lady (49033235647).jpg",
          "caption": "Young lady was selling fish at one of the outlets.\n\nMercado Central, opened in 1872, has piles of fresh fish and crustaceans of local specialties atop mounds of ice. The market is housed in a building in which its main feature is a cast-iron roof and supporting structure. \n\nLocated in the city centre, it is considered a historical landmark and was ranked the fifth best market in the world by the National Geographic. There are a wide variety of stores and places to eat in the market. There is a small fountain in the centre of the market.",
